2026-10-08 10:35:09        "extracted_fact": "The EU Cyber Resilience Act broadens this compliance pressure beyond vehicle-specific approval requirements. The regulation entered into force on December 10, 2024, with full compliance requirements applying from December 11, 2027. Suppliers that provide digital elements incorporated into automotive systems must therefore plan for vulnerability handling, documentation, and security updates alongside automotive functional-safety obligations. The burden is particularly material for smaller software specialists that need to demonstrate compliance across multiple OEM programs without a large in-house assurance organization.\nComplexity and cybersecurity are changing the commercial model of automotive software development. OEMs can no longer treat integration as a final engineering phase once in",
2026-10-08 10:35:09        "excerpt": "The EU Cyber Resilience Act broadens this compliance pressure beyond vehicle-specific approval requirements. The regulation entered into force on December 10, 2024, with full compliance requirements applying from December 11, 2027. Suppliers that provide digital elements incorporated into automotive systems must therefore plan for vulnerability handling, documentation, and security updates alongside automotive functional-safety obligations. The burden is particularly material for smaller software specialists that need to demonstrate compliance across multiple OEM programs without a large in-house assurance organization.\nComplexity and cybersecurity are changing the commercial model of automotive software development. OEMs can no longer treat integration as a final engineering phase once individual suppliers have delivered their components. Architecture decisions, interface governance, security monitoring, update authority, and functional-safety evidence need to be coordinated from the start of a vehicle program.\nThis favors suppliers that can participate in a controlled development ecosystem rather than sell isolated code modules. Middleware providers, operating-system vendors, cybersecurity specialists, and systems integrators gain influence when they reduce interface risk or make compliance evidence reusable. Conversely, fragmented sourcing can preserve purchasing leverage in the short term while increasing the cost and schedule exposure of validation, updates, and incident response after launch.\nAutomotive Software Market Segment Analysis\nApplication software was the largest offering category in 2025, generating USD 9.3 billion. Its scale reflects the breadth of vehicle functions governed by applications, including infotainment, telematics, ADAS, body control, powertrain control, and user-experience features. The segment's approximately 9.4% CAGR is lower than the operating-system and middleware categories because application revenue is spread across a broad inst",
