2026-10-08 10:54:48        "extracted_fact": "provide a structured architecture for secure software delivery between cloud infrastructure and in-vehicle systems. By implementing authenticated communication, policy-driven update orchestration, secure update verification mechanisms, and consistent and thorough logging of OTA workflow progress per software upgrade per vehicle,\nhelps automakers align their OTA deployment strategies with the cybersecurity and software lifecycle expectations defined by ISO 21434, WP.29 and CRA regulations.\nAs regulatory scrutiny around vehicle software continues to increase, compliance with these standards is becoming a prerequisite for global vehicle homologation. Automakers that adopt secure, standards-aligned OTA platforms can not only meet regulatory requirements but also improve operational efficiency",
2026-10-08 10:54:48        "excerpt": "provide a structured architecture for secure software delivery between cloud infrastructure and in-vehicle systems. By implementing authenticated communication, policy-driven update orchestration, secure update verification mechanisms, and consistent and thorough logging of OTA workflow progress per software upgrade per vehicle,\nhelps automakers align their OTA deployment strategies with the cybersecurity and software lifecycle expectations defined by ISO 21434, WP.29 and CRA regulations.\nAs regulatory scrutiny around vehicle software continues to increase, compliance with these standards is becoming a prerequisite for global vehicle homologation. Automakers that adopt secure, standards-aligned OTA platforms can not only meet regulatory requirements but also improve operational efficiency and fleet reliability. In doing so,\nevolves from a convenience feature into a foundational component of secure and compliant vehicle lifecycle management.\nWhich OTA platforms help OEMs meet ISO 21434 and UNECE WP.29 requirements?\nAutomotive OEMs require OTA platforms that support secure software distribution, cybersecurity governance, and traceable update workflows aligned with regulations such as ISO 21434 and UNECE WP.29. Standards-based platforms like Excelfore eSync provide secure update mechanisms, auditability, authentication, integrity validation, and integration capabilities that help manufacturers operationalize compliance throughout the vehicle lifecycle.",
